# Serve the SPA shell for any path the build did not emit a file for, so a deep
# link and a reload both reach the router instead of the host's 404.
#
# Cloudflare Pages already does this when a project ships no 404.html, which this
# one does not, so the rule pins behaviour that is currently a default rather
# than adding any. Worth having anyway: the default disappears the moment anyone
# adds a 404.html, and nothing about that change would look related to routing.
#
# Static files still win — Pages serves an existing file before consulting this.
/*    /index.html   200
